    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305-a1">

                <pb facs="0660" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg576"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 148.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Crook to
                        Adjutant-General Drum.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Department of Arizona, in the Field</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Fort Bowie,<lb/>Arizona</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with instructions contained
                    in your telegram of yesterday, I have the honor to forward herewith the full
                    report of First Lieut. M. P. Maus, First Infantry, of the attack of the Mexican
                    troops on the command of the late Captain Crawford while in camp near the Haros
                    River, Sonora, Mexico, January 11, 1886. The report was received by courier this
                    a.m.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE CROOK,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier-General,
                            Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
